{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>את הכבש האחד</b> — and in Pinchas it is written אחד. Here it is written האחד, which equals 18, hinting at the 18 blessings of prayer that were instituted corresponding to the daily offerings. And there it is written אחד — the count of אחד was that the priests were occupied with the daily offering at times, as stated in Tractate Yoma:" "<b>את הכבש האחד תעשה בבוקר</b> — תעשה: letters תשעה, that nine priests are occupied with the morning daily offering. ואת השני בערב — adds two upon them, for in their hands are two pieces of wood. And here it is written תעשה in singular, while in Pinchas it is written תעשו in plural, to teach that an individual may donate his daily offerings to the public. כבשים הכבש הכבש לכבש הכבש — these are six; they do not fewer than 6 lambs inspected in the Chamber of Lambs, and corresponding to them, 6 occurrences of עולה in the portion of the Akedah:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "The phrase 'כבשים הכבש הכבש לכבש הכבש' lists six forms of the word 'lamb' assembled from verses in the Tamid passage; rendered verbatim as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:44.343085112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}